        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(session-catalog): preserve emoji at long search limits",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where Pi and OpenCode session searches containing emoji near the 500-code-unit limit could be split into malformed Unicode before local matching or paired-node forwarding.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nBoth sibling session catalog plugins now use the existing Plugin SDK UTF-16-safe truncation helper for local and paired-node search terms. This is distinct from #107664, which addresses bounded catalog response JSON; this change is limited to incoming search-term truncation.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers can search local and paired-node Pi and OpenCode sessions with supplementary Unicode characters near the length limit without malformed search strings or incorrect boundary matching.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- AI-assisted: yes. Both sibling implementations and their local and paired-node paths were reviewed.\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/acpx/src/pi-session-catalog.test.ts -t 'keeps local search needles|opens paired-node Pi sessions'` - 2/2 tests passed; 16 skipped.\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/opencode/session-catalog.test.ts -t 'keeps local search needles|marks paired-node sessions'` - 2/2 tests passed; 8 skipped.\n- Tests verify local positive and negative matching plus the exact UTF-16-safe search term forwarded to paired nodes.\n- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD` - passed.\n- Focused validation used the local fallback because Blacksmith Testbox was unavailable and sanitized AWS Crabbox could not acquire a lease.\n- Initial CI run [29359495715](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29359495715) completed. Selected build, type, contract, QA smoke, and test lanes passed. The three failing source checks reproduce only current-base debt outside this PR: an unused Bonjour export, a stale QA Lab max-lines baseline entry, and two over-limit system-agent files.\n",
